# Build 026 M1: these 4 patch files intentionally carry CRLF content lines,
# matching the actual line endings of the upstream cadquery==2.8.0 files
# they patch (scripts/apply-cadquery-novtk-patch.sh applies them verbatim
# with `patch`, which requires the diff's context lines to match the target
# byte-for-byte). The repo-wide `eol=lf` rule above silently normalized them
# to LF in every commit until now — a real, previously undetected defect
# that would have broken patch application on any fresh checkout. `-text`
# disables all line-ending normalization for these specific files.
docs/research/TE-001.1-CadQuery-NoVTK/patches/*.diff -text
